{
  "title": "AI Tools and Tool Instances: Let an Assistant Take Action | CrestApps for Orchard Core",
  "description": "Out of the box, an AI assistant can only talk. Tools let it act: look up an order, search your documentation, list content. This video shows the built-in tools of CrestApps for Orchard Core, who is allowed to use them, and how you create your own tool instances, without code, from ready-made kinds.\n\nIn this video:\n• What a tool is: built-in tools, tool instances, permissions\n• Giving a profile its tools on the Capabilities tab\n• The two permissions: Access any AI tool, and Access AI tool for one tool\n• Creating an HTTP API Request tool instance\n• Using a tool instance in a profile\n• The kinds of tool instances, and sharing tools with other AI apps\n• Use cases",
